{{!-- deploy: the name of the section that lists the build and deploy commands; when set, the last step deploys the apps --}}
Provision the production database once, before the first deploy. Wrangler needs a Cloudflare login first (its `login` command, or `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` in CI).

1. Create the database. `--no-update-config` stops Wrangler from offering to add the binding to `wrangler.jsonc` itself: accepting adds a second binding named after the database next to `DB`, and the code only reads `DB`.

   ```bash
   {{#inDirectory "apps" (deployAppDir)}}{{installedBinaryRunner}} wrangler d1 create {{projectName}}-db --no-update-config{{/inDirectory}}
   ```

2. Copy the `database_id` it prints (not the `binding`, which stays `DB`) into the `d1_databases` entry of {{#if (isMono)}}every `apps/*/wrangler.jsonc` (they all bind this one database){{else}}`wrangler.jsonc`{{/if}}, replacing `REPLACE_WITH_D1_DATABASE_ID`.
{{#if (and (hasRootScript "db:generate") (hasRootScript "db:migrate"))}}

3. Generate the migrations (the template ships none; running `db:generate` again changes nothing when they exist) and apply them to the local database again. Local data is keyed by the `database_id`, so the real id switches local development to a new, empty database: until it is migrated, requests fail with `no such table`. Seed it again only if it held seed data.

   ```bash
   {{runScript "db:generate"}}
   {{runScript "db:migrate"}}
{{#if (hasRootScript "db:seed")}}
   {{runScript "db:seed"}}
{{/if}}
   ```
{{/if}}
{{#if (hasRootScript "db:migrate:remote")}}

{{#if (and (hasRootScript "db:generate") (hasRootScript "db:migrate"))}}4{{else}}3{{/if}}. Apply the migrations to the production database:

   ```bash
   {{runScript "db:migrate:remote"}}
   ```
{{/if}}
{{#if deploy}}

{{#if (and (hasRootScript "db:generate") (hasRootScript "db:migrate"))}}{{#if (hasRootScript "db:migrate:remote")}}5{{else}}4{{/if}}{{else}}{{#if (hasRootScript "db:migrate:remote")}}4{{else}}3{{/if}}{{/if}}. Deploy. A deploy fails until what `wrangler.jsonc` asks for exists, so first:

   - Set the runtime secrets: every name under `secrets.required` in a `wrangler.jsonc` must be set (the secrets notes of the Cloudflare Workers section of `AGENTS.md` say how).
{{#each apps}}
{{#if (appSecrets)}}
     - {{#if (isMono)}}`{{appName}}`: {{/if}}{{#each (appSecrets)}}`{{this}}`{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{/each}}
   - Create every other resource a `wrangler.jsonc` binds (an R2 bucket, a KV namespace), declining Wrangler's offer to add the binding itself as in step 1.
   {{> cloudflare/production-url pointer=true}}

   Then run the build and deploy commands listed under **{{deploy}}**, except `preview`, which keeps running.
{{/if}}
